ic.py`) plus project tests.\nRationale: Verifiable criteria keep the autonomous workflow auditable\nand prevent \"done\" claims that cannot be checked.\n\n### III. Evidence Over Assertion\nClaims about system behavior MUST be labeled as observed evidence\n(command run, output, or test result) or as unverified assertions. A\nclaim of tests passing requires the exact command and its output. No\nevidence, no claim: unresolved or unverified items MUST be recorded\nexplicitly rather than implied.\nRationale: In an autonomous benchmark, unverified assertions are the\nmain source of false completion; evidence discipline makes gaps\nvisible.\n\n### IV. Simple, Scoped Implementations\nImplementations MUST be the smallest change that satisfies the\napproved requirements. No speculative abstractions, configuration\nknobs, or new dependencies beyond the stated scope. Complexity beyond\nthe requirement MUST be justified in the handoff notes; otherwise it\nMUST be removed.\nRationale: The milestone is a single `BatchWriter` class in\n`tinydb/journal.py`; scope creep risks breaking the preserved APIs\nrequired by Principle I.\n\n### V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\nUnresolved assumptions, open questions, and any regressions observed\nduring the work MUST be written into the handoff notes (e.g.\n`HANDOFF.md`) with the evidence or absence of evidence noted. A phase\nMUST NOT close while a known regression is undocumented or\nunmitigated.\nRationale: Later phases run without conversation history; only written\nnotes carry assumptions and regressions forward.\n\n## Project Context (Milestone 1)\n- Project: tinydb, a lightweight pure-Python document database with no\n  external dependencies.\n- Milestone 1 deliverable: `tinydb.journal.BatchWriter(db)` wrapping a\n  supplied `TinyDB` instance, operating on the default table only\n  (`_default`), with atomic batch `apply(operations)` semantics.\n- Feature directory: `/testbed/specs/001-transactions`.\n- Implementation source: `